## PROVENANCE OF THE EVIDENCE (recorded 2026-08-31, at lane-unused's insistence)

Worth pinning, because a ticket this consequential will be re-read by someone
deciding whether to trust it.

**The decisive evidence is a real run, not reasoning.** lane-unused probed with
an explicit coordinator grant at 18:48, staging
`lsp-issue-repro-lsp-b087-probe-zz-control-must-reject` (marker pid 2366987).
The harness staged, attempted `load_plugin`, and the load never reached the
server. The capture below is **the game's own log**, from that run:

    Bytes to read: 73
    Read payload: {"route":"load_plugin","data":{"id":"a","source":"user","type":"
    Bytes to read: 9
    Read payload: folder"}}

Two reads, two requests, two `{"error":"Not implemented: ","data":""}` responses
with an EMPTY route name, because neither fragment parsed.

lane-tooling then independently derived the exact threshold (66 OK / 67 FAIL,
3 trials each with a padded `get_status`) and identified the mechanism in
`HandleClient`. So this ticket rests on **two independent lanes: one live log
capture and one controlled boundary measurement**, which is why the concurrency
framing it was originally filed under could be discarded outright rather than
held as an alternative.

The fixture that run left behind was preserved by B077's fail-closed teardown
(`sweep_stale` correctly refused it as a non-empty marked directory) and was
removed by hand by the lane that owned it, after four checks: marker pid dead,
exactly the three files it staged, byte-identical to source, and ZERO mentions
of its symbols in the game log — i.e. it was never compiled. Plugins dir
verified back to 44 entries.

**That last check is the one worth copying.** "Never compiled" is not inferable
from the filesystem; it took reading the game's log for the fixture's own
symbols. A stranded fixture that WAS compiled is a contaminating installed
plugin; one that never compiled is only litter. Different severities, and only
the log distinguishes them.

## Corrected attribution

An earlier coordinator note on this ticket implied the staging came from an
unexplained code path in the probe harness — some path that stages before
deciding not to probe. **There is no such path.** The lane's "I never took the
game port" statement predated the grant reaching it (messages between sessions
are asynchronous, and it had composed that line before the grant landed); it
then probed with permission and documented the run. Nothing about the harness's
staging behaviour is unaccounted for.